{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '148,177p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '1360,1440p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py; rg -n 'alternative|choice_group|alpha' docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc tests/test_accounting_p03.py | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"\nAll other functions must have a package-registered pure signature and versioned\nimplementation digest; their capability is explicit. Rules may bind values,\ncheck requirements and propose postings. They cannot sample, mutate state or\naccess I/O. Contract and behaviour plugins produce proposed events/state\nchanges through the typed interfaces below. Zero-posting contract changes need\nan explicit non-recognition operation.\n\n## Reconstruction model and finite coverage\n\nA ModelScope lists templates, slots per entity/period, books, account roles,\ntiming/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\noperations. A slot is a possible aggregate event, with an active flag and\nnonnegative amount; inactive implies zero. A template declares both its posting\nincidence vector and economic-state change. Sales and collections are different\nslots; issue and reset are different slots. Debt states retain F/V, rates,\nreset calendar, maturity and hedge links even when historical incidence agrees.\n\nInstantiate every declared slot once, then share variables by economic IDs and\nobservation IDs. Compile roll-forwards and report mappings into constraints;\nadd each accepted evidence domain once. Match source observations by exact\ncontext/mapping, never by label similarity. Attach source/assumption IDs to\nconstraints. Branch on finite choices only, with mutually exclusive guards;\ncontinuous families remain formulas. Count completed, infeasible and unresolved\nchoice cells. `ExactWithinScope` requires every cell decided and each matching\nsource obligation resolved or explicitly outside simulation scope. A satisfied\nwitness alone does not establish coverage. Real-world completeness is never\ninferred from this finite result.\n\nSupported solver fragment: rational linear equalities/inequalities, strict\n                \"uncertainty_kind\": self.bindings.symbol_uncertainty, \"scope\": self.model_id,\n                \"dependencies\": [], \"admission\": f\"admission:{symbol.name}\", \"provenance\": [span_id],\n            })\n        for name in self.lets:\n            self._lower_let(name)\n        # Contract, alternatives, and scenario expressions.\n        contract = next(iter(self.contracts.values()))\n        fields = dict(contract.fields)\n        required_fields = {\"principal\", \"fixed_fraction\", \"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"}\n        if set(fields) != required_fields:\n            self.fail(\"ContractFields\", \"DebtMix requires principal, fraction and two rates\", contract.name)\n        field_rows = []\n        for name in (\"principal\", \"fixed_fraction\", \"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"):\n            expected = {\"principal\": f\"Money<{entity.currency}>\", \"fixed_fraction\": \"Real\",\n                        \"fixed_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple>\", \"initial_floating_rate\": \"Rate<annual_simple>\"}[name]\n            info = self.lower_expr(fields[name], f\"contract:{contract.name}\", f\"field:{name}\", expected)\n            if info[1] != expected:\n                self.fail(\"ContractType\", f\"field {name!r} has type {info[1]}, expected {expected}\", contract.name)\n            if name in {\"fixed_rate\", \"initial_floating_rate\"}:\n                self._assumption_row(f\"contract:{contract.name}:{name}\", info[0], contract.name, evidence)\n            field_rows.append({\"name\": name, \"expression\": info[0]})\n        self.ir[\"contracts\"].append({\"id\": contract.name, \"type\": f\"{package.id}/{contract.type_name}\",\n                                      \"book\": contract.book, \"fields\": field_rows, \"package\": package.id,\n                                      \"source_refs\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]]})\n        alt_ids = []\n        constraint_ids = []\n        for alt in self.alternatives.values():\n            meta = self.bindings.alternative(alt.name)\n            alt_ids.append(alt.name)\n            alt_constraints = []\n            for index, assumption in enumerate(alt.assumptions):\n                eid = self.lower_expr(assumption, f\"alternative:{alt.name}\", f\"assumption:{index}\")[0]\n                cid = f\"constraint:{_clean_id(alt.name)}:{index}\"\n                self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": cid, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                                \"scope\": alt.name, \"source_refs\": []})\n                alt_constraints.append(cid)\n                self._assumption_row(f\"alternative:{alt.name}:{index}\", eid, alt.name, evidence)\n            if not alt_constraints:\n                self.fail(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"named alternatives require a Boolean condition\", alt.name)\n            self.ir[\"alternatives\"].append({\n                \"id\": alt.name, \"parent\": f\"history:{_clean_id(self.model_id)}\", \"scope\": model_scope,\n                \"author\": meta.author,\n                \"created_at\": meta.created_at,\n                \"constraints\": alt_constraints, \"choice_group\": None,\n                \"reason\": meta.reason, \"evidence\": [evidence[next(iter(source_keys.values()))][1]],\n                \"opposing_evidence\": [],\n            })\n        for con in self.constraints.values():\n            eid = self.lower_expr(con.expression, f\"constraint:{con.name}\", \"condition\")[0]\n            self.ir[\"constraints\"].append({\"id\": con.name, \"expression\": eid, \"kind\": \"assumption\",\n                                           \"scope\": model_scope, \"source_refs\": []})\n            constraint_ids.append(con.name)\n            self._assumption_row(f\"constraint:{con.name}\", eid, model_scope, evidence)\n        scenario = next(iter(self.scenarios.values()))\n        settings = dict(scenario.settings)\n        if set(settings) != {\"market_rate\"}:\n            self.fail(\"ScenarioFields\", \"Core0.1 scenario requires one market_rate setting\", scenario.name)\n        driver = self.lower_expr(settings[\"market_rate\"], f\"scenario:{scenario.name}\", \"market_rate\")\n        if not driver[1].startswith(\"Driver<Rate<\"):\n            self.fail(\"ScenarioType\", \"market_rate must be a constant annual rate driver\", scenario.name)\n        self._assumption_row(f\"scenario:{scenario.name}\", driver[0], scenario.name, evidence)\n        self.ir[\"scenarios\"].append({\"id\": scenario.name, \"kind\": \"ExogenousStress\",\n                                      \"drivers\": [{\"name\": \"market_rate\", \"expression\": driver[0]}],\n                                      \"probability_model\": None, \"observed_event\": None, \"structural_model\": None,\n                                      \"replaced_equations\": [], \"visibility\": \"announced\"})\n        # Opening state and report mapping.\n        opening_decl = next(iter(self.openings.values()))\n        opening = self.bindings.opening(opening_decl.external)\n        if opening.book is not None and opening.book != opening_decl.book:\n            self.fail(\"OpeningStateMismatch\", \"opening binding belongs to another book\", opening_decl.name)\n        account_names = {a.name for a in self.accounts.values()}\n        bound_names = {name for name, _ in opening.balances}\n        if account_names != bound_names:\n            self.fail(\"OpeningStateMismatch\", \"opening binding must provide every account exactly once\", opening_decl.name)\n        total = sum((value for _, value in opening.balances), Fraction(0))\n        if total != 0:\n            self.fail(\"UnbalancedState\", \"opening signed balances must sum to zero\", opening_decl.name)\n        self.ir[\"states\"].append({\"id\": opening_decl.name, \"date\": _iso(opening.date, opening_decl.name),\n                                   \"book\": opening_decl.book,\n                                   \"balances\": [{\"account\": name, \"signed_amount\": rational(value)} for name, value in opening.balances],\n                                   \"contracts\": [contract.name], \"measurements\": [],\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:38:alternative fixed { assume share == 1; }\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:39:alternative floating { assume share == 0; }\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:48:    book, symbol = ('Statutory', 'share') if renamed else ('Local', 'alpha')\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:65:            for k in ('alternative','constraint','contract-rate','scenario')],\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:67:        alternatives=[ir.AlternativeBinding(n,'synthetic-author',stamp,'Synthetic endpoint') for n in names],\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:77:        ('BorrowingExample','1','note7','Acme','Local','after2025','debt','alpha','loans',\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:103:    return BASE.replace('contract loans', 'let mix = alpha * 2 / 2;\\nconstraint limit: alpha >= 0 and alpha <= 1;\\ncontract loans').replace(\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:104:        'fixed_fraction = alpha;', 'fixed_fraction = mix;').replace('assume alpha == 1;', 'assume alpha == 1; assume alpha >= 0;').replace(\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:105:        'assume alpha == 0;', 'assume alpha == 0; assume alpha >= 0;')\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:118: 'duplicate_contract_field': (lambda s:s.replace('fixed_fraction = alpha;', 'fixed_fraction = alpha; fixed_fraction = alpha;'),'DuplicateField'),\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:119: 'unknown_reference': (lambda s:s.replace('fixed_fraction = alpha','fixed_fraction = absent'),'UnknownReference'),\ntests/test_accounting_p03.py:121: 'unsupported_call': (lambda s:s.replace('fixed_fraction = alpha','fixed_fraction = sqrt(alpha)'),'UnsupportedExpression'),\ntests/test_accounting_p